1
00:00:49,049 --> 00:00:52,219
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:00:58,934 --> 00:01:00,602
We live within time.

3
00:01:07,401 --> 00:01:09,653
Time doesn't discriminate
between the rich and poor

4
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,280
the good and evil

5
00:01:11,822 --> 00:01:13,657
or the young and the old.

6
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:15,826
Time passes equally for everyone.

7
00:01:50,986 --> 00:01:53,155
I live the time I'm given.

8
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:56,074
Today passes just like yesterday

9
00:01:56,742 --> 00:01:58,201
and tomorrow will be no different.

10
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:01,413
Today, as always

11
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,415
time passes us by

12
00:02:04,374 --> 00:02:05,834
so indifferently.

13
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:47,959
EPISODE 1: GOOD THINGS COME
TO THOSE WHO WAIT

14
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:03,474
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

15
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:04,810
Morning, Ji-hye.

16
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:12,692
- Morning.
- You just got here?

17
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:14,319
Yes, I ran a bit late.

18
00:03:14,945 --> 00:03:16,237
Times have changed.

19
00:03:16,238 --> 00:03:18,156
Good morning, everyone.

20
00:03:18,907 --> 00:03:20,075
Hi, Gong.

21
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:22,993
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

22
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:24,371
- Morning, Gi-tae.
- Hi.

23
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:28,166
- When did you get here?
- Five minutes ago.

24
00:03:39,386 --> 00:03:40,804
Hello, good morning.

25
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:45,726
- You feel okay this morning?
- I'm totally fine.

26
00:03:47,436 --> 00:03:48,854
- Hello, Mr. Jeong.
- Hi.

27
00:03:51,606 --> 00:03:52,690
Hello, Mr. Yang.

28
00:03:52,691 --> 00:03:54,317
- Hello.
- Good morning.

29
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:57,571
- Good morning, Mr. Yang.
- Good morning.

30
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:08,289
- Hey, Ju-hui.
- Good morning.

31
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,666
What happened to the outlet manager
who kicked up a fuss?

32
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,169
- How did you know?
- I know everything.

33
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:15,463
You can run,
but you can't hide from me.

34
00:04:15,464 --> 00:04:16,757
Let's start the meeting.

35
00:04:17,299 --> 00:04:18,341
- Okay.
- Sure.

36
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:29,643
Mr. Yang, it's time for our meeting.

37
00:04:29,644 --> 00:04:31,896
- Coffee?
- Pardon? Well...

38
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:33,731
I think you should come over now.

39
00:04:33,732 --> 00:04:36,318
Can I at least get a coffee
to survive the day?

40
00:04:37,027 --> 00:04:38,361
- Fine, I'm coming.
- Good.

41
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:39,988
I'm coming.

42
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,043
I'll be quick so we can get to work.

43
00:04:54,044 --> 00:04:55,127
- Okay.
- Okay.

44
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,712
Any updates on the discrepancy

45
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:58,798
between the distribution
and what the mall got?

46
00:04:58,799 --> 00:05:01,967
The mall staff forgot to count
a box they had in storage.

47
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:03,762
The numbers add up now.

48
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:06,139
They won't, though.

49
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:08,182
They still resort to borrowing stock

50
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:10,310
from other stores
if the numbers don't add up.

51
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:12,270
You should conduct a spot inspection.

52
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,687
Okay, I'll do that.

53
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:15,106
Why don't we let it drop this time?

54
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:18,651
It's obvious they borrowed stock
from another store.

55
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:21,278
Pointing that out
will only ruffle feathers.

56
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:23,197
Once sales stabilize

57
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:25,158
we can check all the remaining stock.

58
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:28,787
Let's do that, then.

59
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:32,122
I'll revise the schedule
to reflect that.

60
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:34,542
Each brand's
projected spring, summer lineup.

61
00:05:34,543 --> 00:05:36,586
I'd like the full list this week.
Can it be done?

62
00:05:40,465 --> 00:05:43,093
- Mr. Yang.
- I'll tell you when it's ready.

63
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,762
We need the list by this week
so we can review it internally

64
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:48,682
before we place the orders next week.

65
00:05:49,099 --> 00:05:51,726
There's a limit
to what's within my control.

66
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:56,064
Still, check with the brands for me.

67
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:58,608
Okay.

68
00:06:05,574 --> 00:06:07,074
- Ji-hye.
- Yes?

69
00:06:07,075 --> 00:06:09,743
Some brands are changing their CI.
Share the drafts with me

70
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:12,747
and compile a questionnaire
to collect input for a future report.

71
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:14,582
Can you do that by today?

72
00:06:14,583 --> 00:06:15,749
Yes, I can.

73
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,793
Let me know if it's too much.
I'll help.

74
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,296
Not at all. I can manage.

75
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:25,844
There's also concern that employees
are managing their time too freely.

76
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:27,304
The work we do

77
00:06:27,596 --> 00:06:29,847
makes it impossible to work
exactly from nine to six

78
00:06:29,848 --> 00:06:32,683
but I'd like you to follow
company rules as best you can.

79
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:33,976
- Do you all understand?
- Yes.

80
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:34,978
Yes.

81
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,444
- Let's get to work, then.
- Okay.

82
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:45,488
Goodness...

83
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,658
You never get a break, do you?

84
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:51,953
You can train and mentor the juniors

85
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:54,831
but you have one troublemaker
of an assistant manager.

86
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:57,374
Mr. Yang must have
struggles of his own.

87
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:59,835
It can't be easy
working under a younger guy.

88
00:06:59,836 --> 00:07:01,796
True. It's tough on both of you.

89
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:03,798
What's this meeting about?

90
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:07,052
I have no idea
what the higher-ups are thinking.

91
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,346
Oh, shoot.

92
00:07:09,888 --> 00:07:11,013
Where are you going?

93
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:13,349
- It's my leg day.
- What do you mean?

94
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,433
Let's take the stairs.

95
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,852
RESERVATIONS
FOR 4TH-FLOOR CONFERENCE ROOM

96
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:20,190
Hello.

97
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:21,816
Hello.

98
00:07:22,651 --> 00:07:23,652
Hello.

99
00:07:24,653 --> 00:07:26,445
- Mr. Jeong?
- Yes?

100
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,615
Am I a zombie, or are you a rat?

101
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:30,824
What do you mean?

102
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:32,785
Why did you take the stairs

103
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,578
when the elevator
was working just fine?

104
00:07:34,579 --> 00:07:35,664
Oh, you saw us?

105
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:38,958
Mr. Gong and I had
something to discuss.

106
00:07:38,959 --> 00:07:41,794
I wonder if you're still ticked off
because I rejected

107
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:42,796
a few of your ideas.

108
00:07:43,088 --> 00:07:44,506
Did you reject a few ideas?

109
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:46,216
Why don't I remember that?

110
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:47,592
Did he?

111
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:51,972
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

112
00:07:52,681 --> 00:07:54,391
- You're all here.
- Yes.

113
00:07:55,684 --> 00:07:56,935
- You can sit.
- Thanks.

114
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:03,942
Okay.

115
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:07,319
Did you talk to your teams
about managing their time?

116
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,529
- Yes.
- Yes.

117
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:11,657
Someone will get caught first.
Don't let that be you.

118
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:13,325
I can't cover for you then.

119
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:14,493
- Okay.
- Okay.

120
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,787
Let's get things started.

121
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,498
Today's agenda is very simple.

122
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:20,667
Laknes.

123
00:08:24,671 --> 00:08:26,131
What do you all think about it?

124
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:31,970
Shall we go clockwise?

125
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:34,097
Or play rock-paper-scissors?

126
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:41,938
Their designs are one thing,
but their prices are extremely high.

127
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:45,649
They're not that well-known
and have a small collection.

128
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,651
And they don't have
that many patterns, either.

129
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:49,821
I believe
it's a hard brand to launch.

130
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:52,240
What else?

131
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:55,744
I believe they just exited
the Korean market.

132
00:08:56,161 --> 00:09:00,205
Unless they've changed
their designs or pricing

133
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:03,084
won't the result be the same
if we bring them back?

134
00:09:05,378 --> 00:09:07,547
Their designs were hard
to swallow at first.

135
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,631
But times have changed.

136
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,300
They didn't exit
because they flopped.

137
00:09:11,301 --> 00:09:13,677
I think they even got
into the top ten of luxury brands.

138
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:15,680
Didn't they reach ninth?

139
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,308
Yes, just once.

140
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,477
I get what you're all worried about.

141
00:09:20,769 --> 00:09:21,978
We must do this.

142
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:23,688
It's our director's order.

143
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,441
Don't take it. Fight back.

144
00:09:28,193 --> 00:09:30,403
Laknes is known
for its radical designs.

145
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:33,031
Why don't you take it, Mr. Gong?

146
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:35,574
You're the youngest here
and have the best eye for aesthetics.

147
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,576
No?

148
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:44,250
As you know, my team doesn't have
the time or bandwidth.

149
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:47,837
We're the smallest team,
but we handle the most brands.

150
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:50,090
What do the others think?

151
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:52,967
Well...

152
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:56,387
The truth is,
every team is stretched thin.

153
00:09:57,013 --> 00:10:00,517
The team best-suited for the job
would be Mr. Gong's.

154
00:10:01,184 --> 00:10:02,227
You think so too?

155
00:10:04,187 --> 00:10:07,565
I mean, you all have a point

156
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:12,654
but I fear you're giving him too much
because he's the youngest.

157
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:14,572
Then Team 4 should take it.

158
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:17,117
That's not what I meant.

159
00:10:17,826 --> 00:10:19,577
- Mr. Gong.
- Yes?

160
00:10:20,203 --> 00:10:21,538
How about you take Laknes

161
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:25,917
and give a few brands
to some other teams here?

162
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:28,211
Can you do it, then?

163
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:30,713
Yes.

164
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:32,924
Then we can do it.

165
00:10:35,593 --> 00:10:37,470
Stupid, I told you not to take it.

166
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,098
You're out of your mind.

167
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,856
Why did you give in
when I told you not to?

168
00:10:48,857 --> 00:10:50,358
- Whatever.
- Hey.

169
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:53,403
If that's not what you meant,
what did you mean?

170
00:10:53,945 --> 00:10:56,739
I tried to defend you
because they all wanted you to...

171
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:59,284
Gong, can I have a word?

172
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:03,245
Before you hand over
some of your brands

173
00:11:03,246 --> 00:11:05,039
can you talk to me first?

174
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,128
Yes, of course.

175
00:11:10,545 --> 00:11:12,422
- Let's have a drink soon.
- Sure.

176
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:20,638
Mr. Kim.

177
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:24,266
What's this?

178
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:26,226
It got returned.
Give it to your wife.

179
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:28,104
Oh, it's a scarf.

180
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:30,190
Do you think Laknes will work?

181
00:11:30,648 --> 00:11:31,732
Of course not.

182
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:34,694
We're bringing back a brand
that flopped with zero changes.

183
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:38,865
Isn't it a jerk move to dump
a sure-fire flop on another team?

184
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:42,035
I can only go along
with what Mr. Jang suggests.

185
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:43,452
What else can I do?

186
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:45,788
You're way too ambitious.

187
00:11:46,289 --> 00:11:48,791
Why don't you give me something too?

188
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:51,044
What?

189
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:53,295
You want something of mine?

190
00:11:53,296 --> 00:11:57,216
Well, Mr. Jang is in my corner,
but the director is neutral.

191
00:11:57,217 --> 00:11:58,801
I don't feel safe.

192
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:01,511
If Mr. Son gets something
from Mr. Jeong

193
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,972
we'll all be in trouble.

194
00:12:03,973 --> 00:12:05,307
Let's plan long-term.

195
00:12:05,308 --> 00:12:08,269
Give me something good, okay?

196
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:09,938
Thanks for the scarf.

197
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:14,776
Everyone's dead anxious.

198
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:18,154
Laknes is a done deal
because the director wants it

199
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:20,406
but you're the only one
who'll do it without complaint.

200
00:12:20,907 --> 00:12:24,743
They want Kim as associate director,
but his sales aren't good enough

201
00:12:24,744 --> 00:12:27,413
so they're taking a few
of your brands to boost his numbers.

202
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:32,085
And now Son is worried
he won't get promoted this time.

203
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:37,924
And people think I don't care at all
who you give those brands to.

204
00:12:39,133 --> 00:12:41,010
Should I give you one too
if you're that upset?

205
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:44,972
I'm just worried for the two of us.

206
00:12:44,973 --> 00:12:46,140
Don't give me anything.

207
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,600
Here's how I feel.

208
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:50,937
I want my brands to do better
at the new teams.

209
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,897
It's like I want them to meet
a good adoptive family.

210
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,942
Instead of letting them
take what's yours

211
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:58,819
why don't you take a stand?

212
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,739
"I can't take Laknes.
Let me secure my own sales."

213
00:13:03,116 --> 00:13:07,244
Even I think
only I can handle Laknes.

214
00:13:07,245 --> 00:13:08,620
You don't want it, either.

215
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:11,249
Exactly, I don't even want to do it,
so why would you?

216
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:15,002
Since we're on the topic,
think of your poor team.

217
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:17,921
They take all the brands no one wants
and do all the hard work.

218
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,632
Once the brands are on track,
they give them to someone else.

219
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:21,759
What the heck is that?

220
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,053
Are you consoling me or what?

221
00:13:24,846 --> 00:13:28,181
I feel sorry for you, that's all.
I really do.

222
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:31,977
To be honest, no one cares about me

223
00:13:31,978 --> 00:13:34,147
but aren't you in Mr. Jang's camp?

224
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:36,649
What's up with him?

225
00:13:37,025 --> 00:13:39,943
He should be responsible
for the employee he promoted.

226
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,279
Why are you always suffering?

227
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:43,114
Don't you think... What the heck?

228
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:45,742
Gosh, that punk.

229
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:47,493
Wait up.

230
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:52,289
- You're leaving?
- Yes.

231
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,291
Bye.

232
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,755
- Take care, Gong.
- Bye.

233
00:14:09,307 --> 00:14:10,475
I'm heading out.

234
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:12,185
Sure, bye.

235
00:14:14,437 --> 00:14:15,772
Wow, I'm starving.

236
00:14:16,230 --> 00:14:17,689
Let's eat. What do you want?

237
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:21,568
How about the barbecue place
we went to last time?

238
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:23,696
That place is too cheap,
and you're buying.

239
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,365
Oh, am I buying?

240
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,742
Will you join us, Mr. Gong?

241
00:14:29,452 --> 00:14:30,661
No, I'm fine.

242
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:32,913
Okay, I'll head home, then.

243
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:34,499
I'm leaving too, sir.

244
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:38,043
- Let's have what Ji-hye wants.
- Ji-hye?

245
00:14:38,044 --> 00:14:39,544
What I want?

246
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,755
She prefers pork.

247
00:14:41,506 --> 00:14:42,923
- She likes pork?
- Yes.

248
00:14:42,924 --> 00:14:44,759
Then we should go for somaek.

249
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,886
- Somaek.
- Are we getting drunk again?

250
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:49,555
Oh, sounds good.

251
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:59,147
TRAIN IS APPROACHING

252
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,775
STOP

253
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:08,699
What did the doctor say?

254
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:10,575
About your father.

255
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:13,370
Oh, that? He got a few tests done.

256
00:15:13,371 --> 00:15:14,996
The results aren't out yet.

257
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:16,873
But they said
it's nothing to worry about.

258
00:15:16,874 --> 00:15:18,291
Still, keep an eye on him.

259
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:19,960
Older people aren't like
what you think.

260
00:15:19,961 --> 00:15:21,461
Okay, I'll do that.

261
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:22,796
Tell me when you get the results.

262
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:25,216
I can put you in touch
with a different hospital.

263
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:26,843
You'd do that?

264
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:28,928
Thank you.

265
00:15:30,513 --> 00:15:32,097
Are you busy, Ji-hye?

266
00:15:32,098 --> 00:15:33,223
No.

267
00:15:33,224 --> 00:15:34,725
Can you work the tongs, then?

268
00:15:35,226 --> 00:15:36,394
Oh, let me.

269
00:15:36,811 --> 00:15:38,937
I don't mind cooking the meat.

270
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,524
Why? Is it because she's a woman?

271
00:15:42,191 --> 00:15:43,568
Or because she's a contract worker?

272
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:46,487
No, it's not exactly that...

273
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:50,658
Man or woman, contract or full-time,
Ji-hye is still family.

274
00:15:51,409 --> 00:15:52,410
Aren't you the youngest?

275
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:56,539
Yes, I am. I should've
watched the grill. Sorry.

276
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:59,292
I don't know what Gong's thinking

277
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:03,254
but I don't plan to let her go
after her contract expires.

278
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,755
- What?
- Just you wait.

279
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:09,259
I brown-nose everyone
I see at work for a reason.

280
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:10,969
I'm trying to secure an opening.

281
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:13,514
I grovel and beg, just for you.

282
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:17,559
I see. Thank you, Mr. Yang.

283
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,728
If you're grateful,
flip the meat before it burns.

284
00:16:19,729 --> 00:16:20,813
Sorry.

285
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,356
Let's drink.

286
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:16,953
You have a great posture, Mr. Gong.

287
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,706
Don't most office workers

288
00:17:21,707 --> 00:17:24,585
get tech-neck and crooked spines
after seven years?

289
00:17:25,336 --> 00:17:28,047
I have dry eyes and fatty liver,
and that's bad enough for me.

290
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:29,799
You stayed late.

291
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:32,301
This is early for me.

292
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:35,263
You look good.

293
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:37,807
I pretend to be good.

294
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,310
Are you going home?

295
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:43,019
I have plans.

296
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,188
Let's get a drink.

297
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:45,731
I have plans.

298
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,858
Let's have pufferfish soup
and split the bill.

299
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:50,486
I have plans, I said.

300
00:17:51,862 --> 00:17:53,656
You don't have plans.

301
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:57,326
Hurry up.

302
00:17:59,662 --> 00:18:01,079
CHEONGJIN PUFFERFISH

303
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,832
Ma'am, can we get another bottle?

304
00:18:03,374 --> 00:18:05,126
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

305
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:15,803
Hey, why are you always alone?

306
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:19,473
Other team leaders are
always with their minions.

307
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,643
Your team leader
doesn't take you anywhere.

308
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:25,521
I bet it's the same reason.

309
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:27,481
Exactly.

310
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:29,816
I'm asking
since I'm just a member of a team

311
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:32,736
but you're a team leader.

312
00:18:32,737 --> 00:18:34,946
The head of Legal is equivalent
to a managing director

313
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,448
so to be exact, you're above me.

314
00:18:36,449 --> 00:18:37,950
Can you just not?

315
00:18:38,701 --> 00:18:40,452
You treated
everyone from our year to beef

316
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:42,662
because you made team leader.

317
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:44,164
But you're an outcast
in your own team.

318
00:18:44,165 --> 00:18:46,082
You're always
out and about on your own.

319
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:48,377
What was that brand called? Laknes?

320
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:52,172
Why are you letting everyone
play you like a fiddle?

321
00:18:52,173 --> 00:18:54,050
What's the point
of being a team leader?

322
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:58,595
The company has
a big picture for Laknes.

323
00:18:58,596 --> 00:19:02,058
I happen to be
in charge of the backdrop.

324
00:19:02,516 --> 00:19:05,477
Okay. Let's say that
about the company's big picture.

325
00:19:05,478 --> 00:19:08,230
Why is Mr. Yang drawing the picture
for your team?

326
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:11,108
He's always out
with the two underlings.

327
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:15,279
He's making you do all the work
while he plays team leader.

328
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:18,157
I know he joined Hongsung before you

329
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:20,159
but isn't that just wrong?

330
00:19:23,746 --> 00:19:24,872
Mr. Yang...

331
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,086
- He gets on my nerves.
- Right?

332
00:19:31,045 --> 00:19:32,629
But part of me thinks

333
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:35,883
even if he gets on my nerves
and plays team leader

334
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:38,260
if he hits our goals

335
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:42,390
and make things work,
isn't that good enough?

336
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:44,809
We're all there to do a job.

337
00:19:45,518 --> 00:19:47,687
Is it all fine if things work out?

338
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:50,106
You suffer.

339
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,692
If my suffering means things work out

340
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:54,860
it's all good.

341
00:19:55,695 --> 00:19:58,072
Is Hongsung a company or a temple?

342
00:19:58,698 --> 00:20:00,658
You might actually reach nirvana.

343
00:20:10,876 --> 00:20:13,170
See you. Take care at work.

344
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:15,715
You're still talking about work?

345
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:18,467
That's all you talk about.

346
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:21,721
Is your workday not over yet?

347
00:20:22,596 --> 00:20:24,682
Jeez, Gong Eun-tae.

348
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:35,192
Take care.

349
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:17,318
What kind of life am I living?

350
00:21:34,919 --> 00:21:36,212
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

351
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,340
- Let me help.
- No, leave it.

352
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,718
I was born into a family

353
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,012
that wasn't rich,
but wasn't poor, either.

354
00:21:46,931 --> 00:21:48,933
I could climb if I worked hard

355
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:52,269
and I could fall
if I made one mistake.

356
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:54,187
GONG EUN-TAE

357
00:21:54,188 --> 00:21:55,439
That's why I studied hard.

358
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:02,404
I wanted to get
into a better college...

359
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:06,784
and I wanted to get a better job.

360
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:18,462
Regardless of the result,
working hard put me at ease.

361
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:23,509
That's what made me think
I was living life well.

362
00:22:35,271 --> 00:22:38,274
That's how I got a job
at Hongsung International.

363
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:41,652
They have the second-most turnover

364
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:44,196
and the third most brands
in the industry.

365
00:22:44,738 --> 00:22:46,115
It's a large company

366
00:22:46,574 --> 00:22:49,076
with 900 employees
and annual sales of 800 billion won.

367
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:52,329
My parents didn't know
the name of the company

368
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:55,833
but they were proud
I worked at a large one.

369
00:22:56,500 --> 00:23:01,046
And I was grateful I could
support myself before I was too old.

370
00:23:02,673 --> 00:23:05,050
Nothing changed
after I started working.

371
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:08,304
I remained in the same frame

372
00:23:09,430 --> 00:23:10,848
spending the same amount of time

373
00:23:12,099 --> 00:23:13,809
and did my best as always.

374
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:17,396
For three whole years

375
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:21,900
I was the first to come in
and the last to leave.

376
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:23,193
So I got promoted
to assistant manager.

377
00:23:25,279 --> 00:23:27,865
Three more years of that,
and I made team leader.

378
00:23:55,893 --> 00:23:57,227
After all those years of work

379
00:23:57,728 --> 00:24:00,022
I can afford an efficiency apartment

380
00:24:01,732 --> 00:24:04,234
a slightly fatty liver, dry eyes

381
00:24:04,652 --> 00:24:06,528
and an almost slipped disk.

382
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:12,993
Does everyone live like this?

383
00:24:15,913 --> 00:24:17,206
If I work a little harder

384
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:19,333
will my life become a little better?

385
00:24:23,337 --> 00:24:26,006
For what did I live and work so hard?

386
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:37,685
And when did I stop
living and working so hard?

387
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:47,151
- Who is it?
- Hey.

388
00:24:47,152 --> 00:24:48,820
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

389
00:24:48,821 --> 00:24:52,240
- I brought your dry-cleaning.
- Thank you.

390
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:53,825
Oh, one more thing.

391
00:24:53,826 --> 00:24:57,120
I lost one of your dress shirts.

392
00:24:57,121 --> 00:24:58,205
- Did you?
- Yes.

393
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:02,583
Which one did you lose?

394
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:06,587
My wife only said it's in the ledger,
but she can't find it.

395
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:08,382
I don't know which one it is.

396
00:25:08,757 --> 00:25:11,552
Then I guess...

397
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,345
Have a good evening.

398
00:25:19,977 --> 00:25:23,772
And since when did I stop
getting angry?

399
00:25:29,194 --> 00:25:33,115
HANKYEONG BANK
EULJIRO 1-GA STATION

400
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:41,206
Mr. Yang.

401
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:43,583
Hi, Ju-hui.

402
00:25:43,584 --> 00:25:45,794
- Good morning.
- Morning.

403
00:25:47,046 --> 00:25:49,548
Why are you so down this morning?

404
00:25:50,049 --> 00:25:53,010
It's weird to be excited about work.
Beware of such people.

405
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:56,972
Are you worried
about the brand shift?

406
00:25:58,724 --> 00:26:01,018
The brand shift? What do you mean?

407
00:26:01,727 --> 00:26:03,228
You haven't heard?

408
00:26:07,858 --> 00:26:09,610
- Morning.
- Hello.

409
00:26:11,904 --> 00:26:13,238
Good morning.

410
00:26:15,032 --> 00:26:16,867
- Mr. Yang.
- Hello.

411
00:26:17,451 --> 00:26:19,745
- Morning. Can you...
- Let's talk.

412
00:26:41,183 --> 00:26:43,727
What is this about?

413
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:48,023
What's this about handing over
our brands to other teams?

414
00:26:52,027 --> 00:26:53,112
Stuff happened.

415
00:26:53,487 --> 00:26:54,571
Yes, but why?

416
00:26:57,032 --> 00:26:59,200
We have to launch Laknes.

417
00:26:59,201 --> 00:27:01,577
We have to start from scratch

418
00:27:01,578 --> 00:27:02,913
and it'll be a lot of work.

419
00:27:03,539 --> 00:27:08,210
So we have to pack up the brands
we were working on

420
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:11,380
so other teams can take over.

421
00:27:13,423 --> 00:27:15,384
Don't you think that's too much?

422
00:27:17,136 --> 00:27:20,848
None of our previous brands
started off normal.

423
00:27:21,807 --> 00:27:22,850
Eynard?

424
00:27:24,393 --> 00:27:27,436
They made a decent amount,
and Team 3 couldn't handle it.

425
00:27:27,437 --> 00:27:29,648
So they were fine,
but what about the others?

426
00:27:30,732 --> 00:27:32,776
Weren't they all brands
that should've been dropped?

427
00:27:33,694 --> 00:27:36,362
We took them in and revived them

428
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:37,613
only to lose them.

429
00:27:37,614 --> 00:27:40,325
Now we get Laknes
that flopped once already?

430
00:27:40,951 --> 00:27:43,370
Even if the team leader
doesn't have much clout

431
00:27:44,204 --> 00:27:46,373
that doesn't mean
they can walk all over the team.

432
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:50,669
Mr. Yang.

433
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:55,716
Do you think
I want to lose the brands

434
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:58,427
I was working on?

435
00:27:59,553 --> 00:28:00,596
Mr. Gong.

436
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:06,058
Can you please do
just one thing for me?

437
00:28:06,059 --> 00:28:08,270
Let us keep our projects.

438
00:28:08,562 --> 00:28:12,608
That's the least you can do
if you expect us to trust you.

439
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,194
Is that so much to ask?

440
00:28:17,196 --> 00:28:20,073
Just let us do our job in peace.

441
00:28:20,991 --> 00:28:22,034
Please?

442
00:29:02,908 --> 00:29:04,243
Did Mr. Yang headbutt you?

443
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:08,872
That stupid punk.

444
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:14,211
He was right, though.

445
00:29:15,254 --> 00:29:17,798
A team leader is useless
if he loses his team's trust.

446
00:29:18,173 --> 00:29:20,884
So what? If Yang headbutted you

447
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:22,302
what will you do?

448
00:29:22,928 --> 00:29:24,805
Shouldn't you headbutt someone too?

449
00:29:27,808 --> 00:29:30,060
Did you ever see me get angry?

450
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:33,355
Have I seen you get angry?

451
00:29:34,189 --> 00:29:35,190
I haven't.

452
00:29:35,983 --> 00:29:37,651
I don't shout when I'm angry.

453
00:29:38,694 --> 00:29:41,738
If I do, I only have to sort out
that aftermath.

454
00:29:42,614 --> 00:29:46,075
No one cares about that
when they're angry.

455
00:29:46,076 --> 00:29:47,744
They just lash out.

456
00:29:51,581 --> 00:29:53,875
So what? What will you do now?

457
00:29:54,710 --> 00:29:56,086
I must do something.

458
00:29:56,962 --> 00:29:58,088
Like what?

459
00:29:58,547 --> 00:30:00,048
ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

460
00:30:08,348 --> 00:30:10,225
- Is he in?
- Yes.

461
00:30:22,738 --> 00:30:23,780
Come in.

462
00:30:32,164 --> 00:30:33,165
What is it?

463
00:30:33,749 --> 00:30:35,125
I have something to say.

464
00:30:35,417 --> 00:30:37,586
- Will it take a while?
- It might.

465
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:39,546
Sit.

466
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,681
What is it?

467
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:52,893
It's about Laknes.

468
00:30:53,310 --> 00:30:55,103
Could you give it to another team?

469
00:30:59,149 --> 00:31:02,027
Is your team disheartened
about taking Laknes?

470
00:31:04,071 --> 00:31:05,364
Did Yang Jun-ho complain?

471
00:31:08,450 --> 00:31:09,992
Talk to me.

472
00:31:09,993 --> 00:31:13,246
He's the only subordinate
who would complain.

473
00:31:14,039 --> 00:31:17,042
Everyone agrees, though.

474
00:31:33,183 --> 00:31:34,184
Hey.

475
00:31:36,019 --> 00:31:37,896
Will you let them
control you forever?

476
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:42,691
If you really can't do it,
then I'll accept that.

477
00:31:42,692 --> 00:31:44,194
I can give it to another team.

478
00:31:44,861 --> 00:31:46,029
But that's not the case.

479
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:49,740
You can take it,
but one of your lackeys can't.

480
00:31:49,741 --> 00:31:52,619
Isn't that why you took a deep breath
before coming in to see me?

481
00:31:53,829 --> 00:31:56,373
Do you think I made you team leader
to take on easy jobs?

482
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:01,420
No, I never thought so.

483
00:32:04,131 --> 00:32:06,341
Jeez, that's exactly what you think.

484
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:12,931
It's easy to keep doing
what you're good at.

485
00:32:13,348 --> 00:32:15,516
As long as your brain works

486
00:32:15,517 --> 00:32:17,978
anyone can do that. However...

487
00:32:20,021 --> 00:32:22,065
It's hard to revive a dying brand.

488
00:32:23,233 --> 00:32:24,901
That's not for just anyone.

489
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:28,363
I gave you the job
because I believe in you.

490
00:32:29,156 --> 00:32:30,782
Yes, it will be hard work.

491
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:33,951
And your team will complain,
but what can I do?

492
00:32:33,952 --> 00:32:36,705
They pull off
what you tell them to do.

493
00:32:41,668 --> 00:32:42,669
Bear with it.

494
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:46,423
And pull it off.

495
00:32:46,840 --> 00:32:48,091
It goes on your record.

496
00:32:53,388 --> 00:32:54,473
Get out of here.

497
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:23,210
Darn it.

498
00:33:25,378 --> 00:33:26,837
- Gi-tae.
- Yes?

499
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:29,424
- Let's go out for a smoke.
- Okay.

500
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:32,677
Ji-hye, join us for some air.

501
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:34,429
Okay.

502
00:33:35,096 --> 00:33:36,515
Jeez...

503
00:34:05,585 --> 00:34:08,629
PRESSED PORK HEAD MEAT

504
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:10,757
KOREAN BEEF

505
00:34:15,220 --> 00:34:18,348
SEONGGYEONG BUTCHER

506
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:29,859
SYSTEM IS DOWN

507
00:34:31,695 --> 00:34:32,696
SYSTEM IS DOWN

508
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:37,075
Sorry, the checkout machine
isn't working.

509
00:34:37,951 --> 00:34:39,703
What should I do, then?

510
00:34:40,579 --> 00:34:41,705
Do you have cash?

511
00:34:42,539 --> 00:34:43,540
Yes.

512
00:34:47,502 --> 00:34:49,379
- Here.
- That's 10,000 won.

513
00:34:57,429 --> 00:34:58,763
We're out of change.

514
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:00,724
I'll come by another time.

515
00:35:04,436 --> 00:35:05,854
Would you like to buy
a lottery ticket?

516
00:35:07,272 --> 00:35:08,273
Sorry?

517
00:35:08,565 --> 00:35:11,359
Two beers are 5,000 won,
and a ticket is 5,000 won.

518
00:35:14,696 --> 00:35:16,531
- Sure, give me one.
- Okay.

519
00:35:22,662 --> 00:35:23,747
Random numbers?

520
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,458
Okay.

521
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:33,840
Here you go.

522
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:43,058
Do I get a plastic bag?

523
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:45,935
You didn't pay 100 won for one.

524
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:28,019
MOM

525
00:36:32,607 --> 00:36:33,733
Hello, Mom.

526
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:35,485
Did you have dinner?

527
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:37,695
I'm eating right now.

528
00:36:37,696 --> 00:36:39,239
Do you have any food at home?

529
00:36:39,614 --> 00:36:41,116
Should I send you some?

530
00:36:41,533 --> 00:36:44,284
I still have what you sent me
last time.

531
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:46,328
I sent that a long time ago.

532
00:36:46,329 --> 00:36:47,455
You should eat it up quickly.

533
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:51,292
Tell me if you ever need
any side dishes.

534
00:36:51,751 --> 00:36:53,544
I'll tell you if I do.

535
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:55,922
Okay. Oh, there's one more thing.

536
00:36:56,172 --> 00:36:58,425
It's nothing serious.

537
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:01,469
Can you give your brother
five million won?

538
00:37:03,388 --> 00:37:04,888
What is it this time?

539
00:37:04,889 --> 00:37:08,642
Your brother was on the night shift

540
00:37:08,643 --> 00:37:10,894
and some drunkards got into a fight.

541
00:37:10,895 --> 00:37:14,314
When Eun-seok tried to stop them,
one guy fell and hurt his back.

542
00:37:14,315 --> 00:37:17,359
He's demanding your brother
pay for the treatment

543
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:18,694
but you know he's penniless.

544
00:37:18,695 --> 00:37:22,323
A security guard barely makes enough
after expenses and his kid's tuition.

545
00:37:22,824 --> 00:37:24,074
I'll give him a call.

546
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:25,826
No, don't call him.

547
00:37:25,827 --> 00:37:28,246
He doesn't know I called you.

548
00:37:28,788 --> 00:37:30,165
He knows.

549
00:37:30,749 --> 00:37:32,125
I'll call him.

550
00:37:40,550 --> 00:37:42,302
GONG EUN-SEOK

551
00:37:43,303 --> 00:37:44,804
CALLING

552
00:37:45,430 --> 00:37:48,099
MY LITTLE BROTHER

553
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:58,943
Hey, Eun-tae.

554
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:01,070
You need money?

555
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:03,865
Gosh, did Mom tell you?

556
00:38:04,741 --> 00:38:06,367
I told her not to tell you.

557
00:38:07,076 --> 00:38:08,619
Will five million won do?

558
00:38:08,620 --> 00:38:10,245
Yes, that'll be enough.

559
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:12,623
I'll pay you back soon.

560
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:13,750
When?

561
00:38:14,584 --> 00:38:16,085
What? When?

562
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:19,087
When can I pay you back?

563
00:38:19,088 --> 00:38:20,339
Let me see...

564
00:38:20,340 --> 00:38:22,550
Do you know
how much I lent you so far?

565
00:38:24,302 --> 00:38:26,679
Just ask for it.
Why do you say you owe me?

566
00:38:27,430 --> 00:38:30,098
But I should pay you back.

567
00:38:30,099 --> 00:38:31,100
Eun-seok.

568
00:38:31,851 --> 00:38:35,313
Do you think everyone
with an office job can save up?

569
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:37,357
I don't have much.

570
00:38:38,024 --> 00:38:41,069
Do you know how much it costs
to just live and breathe in Seoul?

571
00:38:43,363 --> 00:38:45,240
We're family, aren't we?

572
00:38:46,950 --> 00:38:48,117
If we can't help each other

573
00:38:49,369 --> 00:38:50,912
let's at least not burden each other.

574
00:38:53,081 --> 00:38:54,833
Okay. Sorry.

575
00:38:56,668 --> 00:38:59,420
- I'll wire it right now.
- Oh, thanks.

576
00:39:04,509 --> 00:39:05,592
TYPE YOUR PIN

577
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:08,054
5,000,000 WON SENT TO GONG EUN-SEOK

578
00:39:50,138 --> 00:39:52,015
SUPPLEMENT FOR STOMACH LINING

579
00:40:56,621 --> 00:40:57,664
SWOOSH

580
00:41:20,061 --> 00:41:24,065
6 LOTTERY WINNERS THIS WEEK
EACH GETS 1.9 BILLION WON

581
00:41:41,582 --> 00:41:43,960
LOTTO
5609TH DRAWING

582
00:42:07,483 --> 00:42:11,237
CONGRATULATIONS
TOTAL WINNINGS: 1,977,507,240 WON

583
00:42:13,823 --> 00:42:18,745
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

584
00:42:42,435 --> 00:42:44,729
I've had enough for the day.

585
00:42:45,229 --> 00:42:46,438
Are you going home?

586
00:42:46,439 --> 00:42:49,317
Yes, if I stay any longer,
I feel like I might die.

587
00:42:50,735 --> 00:42:51,819
I feel the same.

588
00:42:52,153 --> 00:42:53,528
Why are you still here?

589
00:42:53,529 --> 00:42:55,865
If I leave now, I'll die tomorrow.

590
00:42:56,783 --> 00:42:58,576
We all live one day at a time.

591
00:42:59,368 --> 00:43:01,120
Wrap it up quickly.

592
00:43:01,788 --> 00:43:02,789
Have a good night.

593
00:43:15,510 --> 00:43:18,971
THIS WEEK'S TASKS

594
00:44:30,293 --> 00:44:34,297
GOT OFF WORK YET?

595
00:44:39,510 --> 00:44:41,512
GONG EUN-TAE

